@author "Claude (Anthropic)"

; The same fold with a bare toward measures every object of the alignment,
; the part of --h as well. Both candidates land a part of --h on the lower
; half of --v, equally near .u, so the selection names no line and the hint
; names what to measure (ADR 0031).

paper square
mark (map .a onto .b) as --v
mark (map .a onto .d) as --h
.u = free on --ab from .b at 1/5
fold (map --v onto --h) (toward .u)

; expect error "toward .u lies as near to where one fold of map --v onto --h lands the objects of its alignments as to where another does"
